# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  freejarvis — copy this to .env and pick a brain.
#
#  There are two ways to give it one, and you only need either.
#  The default is a free hosted model: no GPU, no download, no
#  credit card. Getting a key takes about a minute.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. Attach a Hermes Agent ─────────────────────────────────
# The good path, if you already self-host one. freejarvis becomes
# its face: its sessions, cron jobs, skills, toolsets and
# approvals, all live.
#
# Hermes' API server is off by default. In ~/.hermes/.env:
#   API_SERVER_ENABLED=true
#   API_SERVER_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# then run `hermes gateway`.
#
# You do NOT need to configure CORS. Every call goes through this
# server, not your browser — which is also why the key never
# reaches the page. `localhost` is rewritten to
# host.docker.internal inside the container automatically.
#
# HERMES_URL=http://localhost:8642
# HERMES_KEY=


# ── 2. Or talk to a model directly ───────────────────────────
# Used when no agent is attached. Anything that speaks the
# OpenAI chat-completions shape works: Ollama, LM Studio,
# llama.cpp, vLLM, OpenRouter, Groq, Cerebras, Together,
# Google AI Studio, OpenAI itself.
#
# Free key (no card): https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Free models are the ones ending in `:free`.
LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
LLM_MODEL=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free
LLM_API_KEY=

# Groq — free, and very fast
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# Cerebras — free, high daily token allowance
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.cerebras.ai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b

# Fully local — nothing leaves your machine.
# OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH is not optional: Ollama defaults to 4096
# tokens and truncates longer prompts *silently*.
#   OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=16384 ollama serve
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:7b

# Anthropic — point the base URL here and freejarvis switches
# wire format on its own: x-api-key instead of Bearer, the
# version header, the system prompt hoisted out of the message
# list, tool results as content blocks. You configure none of it.
# Written and unit-tested; never exercised against the live API.
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5


# ── Optional: a voice worth listening to ─────────────────────
# Without a key it speaks through your browser: free, offline,
# and it sounds like it. With one it sounds like a product — and
# the orb gets better too, because a real audio stream can be
# measured rather than guessed at.
#
# This is a paid service. It is opt-in and never required.
# Keys: https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=onwK4e9ZLuTAKqWW03F9   # Daniel — British, steady
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_turbo_v2_5         # eleven_flash_v2_5 is faster, thinner
# ELEVENLABS_SPEED=1.12                      # 0.7–1.2


# ── Optional: sites it can pull up ───────────────────────────
# A folder of .html files. Every one becomes something you can
# ask for out loud, by name.
# SITES_DIR=/absolute/path/to/your/sites


# ── Optional: the shell tool ─────────────────────────────────
# Off unless you turn it on, and even on it asks before every
# command. A web page that can run commands on your host is a
# different threat model to one that can read a file.
# FREEJARVIS_SHELL=1
